From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: sunxi: sun50i-di300: fix Cr from semi-planar input,
 open the TNR window

A semi-planar source (NV12/NV21/NV16/NV61) with a planar capture format
came out with a broken Cr plane: every line held the first Cr line of
its field. The engine reads Cb and Cr of an interleaved chroma plane
through two channels and steps the Cr one by the third input pitch,
which the driver left at zero for these formats. Set it to the chroma
stride, as the vendor driver does.

TNR changed only the top left pixel. The TNR block filters only inside
its demo window (0x2a8/0x2ac), which has no enable bit; the driver
cleared it to an empty window. Open it to the full frame on every TNR
job, as the vendor does (its tnr_demo_crop defaults to the output crop).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c         | 24 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
@@ -155,8 +155,15 @@ static void deinterlace_get_planes(const struct v4l2_pix_format *fmt,
 		}
 		break;
 	default:
-		/* UV-combined formats: no separate third plane */
+		/*
+		 * UV-combined formats: no separate third plane, but the
+		 * engine still steps its Cr line address by the third pitch
+		 * (with zero, a planar capture format got the first Cr line
+		 * of each field in every line). The vendor sets it to the
+		 * chroma stride for these formats too.
+		 */
 		pl->pitch[1] = bpl;
+		pl->pitch[2] = bpl;
 		break;
 	}
 }
@@ -667,6 +674,19 @@ static void deinterlace_device_run(void *priv)
 	deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_MD_CROP_V, reg);
 	deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_TNR_CROP_V, reg);
 
+	/*
+	 * The TNR filters only inside its demo window, which has no enable
+	 * bit: a zero window filtered the top left pixel alone. Open it to
+	 * the full frame, as the vendor does (tnr_demo_crop = the output
+	 * crop).
+	 */
+	if (ctx->tnr_active) {
+		reg = (ctx->src_fmt.width - 1) << 16;
+		deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_TNR_DEMO_H, reg);
+		reg = (ctx->src_fmt.height - 1) << 16;
+		deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_TNR_DEMO_V, reg);
+	}
+
 	if (ctx->fmd_active) {
 		reg = (ctx->src_fmt.width - 1) << 16;
 		deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_FMD_CROP_H, reg);
@@ -1012,8 +1032,6 @@ static void deinterlace_init(struct deinterlace_dev *dev)
 		deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_TNR_RANDOM_CFG, 0x02031c01);
 		deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_TNR_RANDOM_GEN, 0);
 		deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_TNR_MD_RESULT, 0);
-		deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_TNR_DEMO_H, 0);
-		deinterlace_write(dev, DEINTERLACE_TNR_DEMO_V, 0);
 	}
 }
 
